      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "content": "# Polaris Processors\n\nMetrics from `libs/pipeline/src/metrics.ts`, exposed at each processor's `/metrics` endpoint. Each processor gets an explicit job in `infra/prometheus/prometheus.yml`; new ones join the same scrape pattern.\n\n**Per-processor row.** The template variable `$processor_name` selects one of `sync-identity-resolver`, `sync-enrichment-runtime`, `sessionizer`, `attribution-engine`, `merge-worker`. Pick `All` to see the fleet aggregate.\n\n**Latency.** `polaris_processor_lag_seconds` and `polaris_processor_handler_duration_seconds` are histograms (CSH8YAL6); the p50/p99 panels at the bottom of the dashboard use them. The legacy `_ms_last` gauges are kept alongside during the transition for the `max` / `lastNotNull` panels \u2014 feel free to favour the histogram panels.\n\n**DLQ backlog.** DLQ growth is shown as a **rate**, not as the dead-letter table's total backlog. For a true backlog gauge, query the `processor_dlq_records` table directly via the DLQ triage runbook (P10-006).",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.4.0",
      "title": "About this dashboard",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10
          },
          "unit": "ops"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6
      },
      "id": 2,
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "calcs": ["mean", "max"]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.4.0",
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (processor_name) (rate(polaris_processor_events_consumed_total{processor_name=~\"$processor_name\", environment=\"$environment\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{processor_name}} \u2014 consumed",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Events consumed (5m, ops)",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
